.TH SDL_HINT_MOUSE_RELATIVE_SYSTEM_SCALE 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_HINT_MOUSE_RELATIVE_SYSTEM_SCALE \- A variable controlling whether the system mouse acceleration curve is used for relative mouse motion.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_hints.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_HINT_MOUSE_RELATIVE_SYSTEM_SCALE \(dqSDL_MOUSE_RELATIVE_SYSTEM_SCALE\(dq
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The variable can be set to the following values:
.PP

\(bu \(dq0\(dq: Relative mouse motion will be unscaled\[char46] (default)
.PP
\(bu \(dq1\(dq: Relative mouse motion will be scaled using the system mouse acceleration curve\[char46]
.PP
If
.BR SDL_HINT_MOUSE_RELATIVE_SPEED_SCALE
is set, that will be applied after system speed scale\[char46]
.PP
This hint can be set anytime\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This hint is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

